{{template "head" .}}
<section class="features">
  <div class="container"><div class="spacer">
    <h1>Documentation</h1>
    <div class="fx">
      <div class="c-lg-6 c-xs-12">
        <h2 class="sub">1. Run the NSM backend</h2>
        <p>Double-click <strong>NSM-Masterlist.exe</strong> (or run it from a terminal). It serves the website, accounts, server list and game cache on <code>http://127.0.0.1</code>.</p>
        <h2 class="sub">2. Play</h2>
        <p>Open <strong>NSM.exe</strong>, browse servers at <code>http://127.0.0.1/servers</code> or in the client, and join.</p>
        <h2 class="sub">3. Run your own server</h2>
        <p>Unzip NSM Server, configure <code>server.cfg</code>, start <strong>NSM-Server.exe</strong>. Your server appears on the list automatically.</p>
        <h2 class="sub">4. Owner tools</h2>
        <p>Log in as the owner account, then use <a href="/admin/users">Staff &amp; users</a> to manage roles.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="c-lg-6 c-xs-12">
        <h2 class="sub">System requirements</h2>
        <table class="stat-table">
          <tr><td><span class="stat">OS</span></td><td>Windows 10 or 11</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="stat">CPU</span></td><td>Intel Core i5-3470 / AMD FX-8350 (server: any quad-core)</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="stat">GPU</span></td><td>NVIDIA GTX 660 2GB / AMD HD 7870 2GB</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="stat">RAM</span></td><td>8GB</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="stat">Disk</span></td><td>GTA V (~105GB) + ~4GB NSM</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="stat">Game</span></td><td>Grand Theft Auto V (any edition)</td></tr>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div></div>
</section>
{{template "foot" .}}
